# Oxidized device source — CSV, colon-delimited: name:model:ip:username:password
# Lives at /opt/oxidized/.config/oxidized/router.db on CA-OXI-LAB, mode 0600.
#
# Per-node credentials. Originally three fields, with one global admin
# credential in the main config. When the fleet moved to TACACS+, that global
# credential broke each device as it was converted — so every device got its own
# entry, and moved to the read-only service account as it was converted. Once
# all six had moved, the global fallback was deleted from the main config.
#
# The map for these columns is in the `source:` block of the main config.
#
# No per-device algorithm columns. All six devices — including the 2003
# Catalyst 2940 that offers only diffie-hellman-group1-sha1 — negotiate with
# net-ssh's defaults. The legacy-crypto overrides needed for interactive
# OpenSSH are an OpenSSH client policy, not a device limitation.
#
# Per-model settings (Arista enable / auth_methods) live in the `models:`
# block of the main config, not here, so that booleans stay booleans.
3560CG-1:ios:10.99.10.1:svc-oxidized:<SERVICE_ACCOUNT_PASSWORD>
3560CG-2:ios:10.99.20.1:svc-oxidized:<SERVICE_ACCOUNT_PASSWORD>
C2940-LAB:ios:10.99.20.20:svc-oxidized:<SERVICE_ACCOUNT_PASSWORD>
ARISTA710P-LAB:eos:10.99.10.14:svc-oxidized:<SERVICE_ACCOUNT_PASSWORD>
SRX345-LAB:junos:10.99.0.2:svc-oxidized:<SERVICE_ACCOUNT_PASSWORD>
PA440-LAB:panos:10.99.0.1:svc-oxidized:<SERVICE_ACCOUNT_PASSWORD>
